{"title":"1991 AJHSME Problems/Problem 14","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Several students are competing in a series of three races.  A student earns <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> points for winning a race, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> points for finishing second and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> point for finishing third.  There are no ties.  What is the smallest number of points that a student must earn in the three races to be guaranteed of earning more points than any other student?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/2/14285a1bef65939f9f378a3ec77625a01cab6fd1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 9 \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ 10 \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ 11 \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 13 \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"366\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>It is possible for two students to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> points: one student could win the first two races and finish third in the third race (scoring <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/7/23769b23072bbed9c608b057a4401a6a46ec1d12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5+5+1=11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"116\" height=\"15\" />), while another student could finish second in the first two races and win the third race (scoring <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/c/edc823394173b7d76ce683147715dce795c78691.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3+3+5=11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"116\" height=\"15\" />).\n</p><p>To score <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> or more points, a student must win at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> races. So any other student could win at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> race and thus score at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/1/691e71b60c2ef47d369d966a215b00b4ba6949e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 + 3 + 3 = 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"116\" height=\"15\" /> points.  Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/e/b6edad35ff25693154ce21d1b9568e7dc6c6f34f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"65\" height=\"28\" /> is the minimum score a student needs to guarantee outscoring all other students.\n</p><p>Note: it is impossible for a student to score exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> points. \n</p><p>-stjwyl, edited by j314andrews\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AJHSME\" title=\"1991 AJHSME\">1991 AJHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AJHSME_Problems\" title=\"1991 AJHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AJHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1991 AJHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=1991\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1991 AJHSME Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1991 AJHSME Problems/Problem 15\">Problem 15</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1991 AJHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1991 A